      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we start by understanding the given information. Let \\( N \\) be the integer. We are told that when \\( N \\) is divided by 15, the remainder is 7. This can be expressed mathematically as:\n\\[ N = 15k + 7 \\]\nwhere \\( k \\) is an integer.\n\nThe first part of the problem asks for the sum of the remainders when \\( N \\) is divided by 3 and by 5. To find these remainders, we need to consider the expression for \\( N \\) modulo 3 and modulo 5.\n\n1. **Modulo calculations:**\n   - For division by 3, note:\n     \\[ N \\equiv 7 \\pmod{3} \\]\n     Since 7 modulo 3 is:\n     \\[ 7 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}, \\]\n     we can see that the remainder when \\( N \\) is divided by 3 is 1.\n\n   - For division by 5, note:\n     \\[ N \\equiv 7 \\pmod{5} \\]\n     Since 7 modulo 5 is:\n     \\[ 7 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{5}, \\]\n     we can see that the remainder when \\( N \\) is divided by 5 is 2.\n\n2. **Summing the remainders:**\n   The sum of the remainders 1 and 2 is:\n   \\[ 1 + 2 = 3. \\]\n\nThus, the remainder when \\( N \\) is divided by 3 added to the remainder when \\( N \\) is divided by 5 is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3}\n\\]",
